<http://w3id.org/cacao/shapes/P9_consists_of> a sh:PropertyShape ;
    rdfs:label "P9 setzt sich zusammen aus"@de,
        "P9 αποτελείται από"@el,
        "P9 consists of"@en,
        """Quantification: many to many (0,n:0,n)

Scope note:
This property associates an instance of E4 Period with another instance of E4 Period that is defined by a subset of the phenomena that define the former. Therefore, the spacetime volume of the latter must fall within the spacetime volume of the former.
This property is transitive and asymmetric.

Examples:
- Cretan Bronze Age (E4) consists of Middle Minoan (E4). (Hood, 1971)

In First Order Logic:
- P9(x,y) ⇒ E4(x)
- P9(x,y) ⇒ E4(y)
- P9(x,y) ⇒ P10(y,x)
- [P9(x,y) ∧ P9(y,z)] ⇒ P9(x,z)
- P9(x,y) ⇒ ¬P9(y,x)
"""@en,
        "P9 comprend"@fr,
        "P9 consiste de"@pt,
        "P9 состоит из"@ru,
        "P9 包括"@zh ;
    sh:class <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E4_Period> ;
    sh:description """Quantification: many to many (0,n:0,n)

Scope note:
This property associates an instance of E4 Period with another instance of E4 Period that is defined by a subset of the phenomena that define the former. Therefore, the spacetime volume of the latter must fall within the spacetime volume of the former.
This property is transitive and asymmetric.

Examples:
- Cretan Bronze Age (E4) consists of Middle Minoan (E4). (Hood, 1971)

In First Order Logic:
- P9(x,y) ⇒ E4(x)
- P9(x,y) ⇒ E4(y)
- P9(x,y) ⇒ P10(y,x)
- [P9(x,y) ∧ P9(y,z)] ⇒ P9(x,z)
- P9(x,y) ⇒ ¬P9(y,x)
"""@en ;
    sh:name "P9 setzt sich zusammen aus"@de,
        "P9 αποτελείται από"@el,
        "P9 consists of"@en,
        "P9 comprend"@fr,
        "P9 consiste de"@pt,
        "P9 состоит из"@ru,
        "P9 包括"@zh ;
    sh:nodeKind sh:BlankNodeOrIRI ;
    sh:path <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P9_consists_of> .

<http://w3id.org/cacao/shapes/P9i_forms_part_of> a sh:PropertyShape ;
    rdfs:label "P9i bildet Teil von"@de,
        "P9i αποτελεί μέρος του/της"@el,
        "P9i forms part of"@en,
        """Quantification of the inverse property: many to many (0,n:0,n)

Scope note of the inverse property:
This property associates an instance of E4 Period with another instance of E4 Period that is defined by a subset of the phenomena that define the former. Therefore, the spacetime volume of the latter must fall within the spacetime volume of the former.
This property is transitive and asymmetric.

Examples of the inverse property:
- Cretan Bronze Age (E4) consists of Middle Minoan (E4). (Hood, 1971)

In First Order Logic of the inverse property:
- P9(x,y) ⇒ E4(x)
- P9(x,y) ⇒ E4(y)
- P9(x,y) ⇒ P10(y,x)
- [P9(x,y) ∧ P9(y,z)] ⇒ P9(x,z)
- P9(x,y) ⇒ ¬P9(y,x)
"""@en,
        "P9i fait partie de"@fr,
        "P9i faz parte de"@pt,
        "P9i являeтся частью"@ru,
        "P9i 组成部分"@zh ;
    sh:class <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E4_Period> ;
    sh:description """Quantification of the inverse property: many to many (0,n:0,n)

Scope note of the inverse property:
This property associates an instance of E4 Period with another instance of E4 Period that is defined by a subset of the phenomena that define the former. Therefore, the spacetime volume of the latter must fall within the spacetime volume of the former.
This property is transitive and asymmetric.

Examples of the inverse property:
- Cretan Bronze Age (E4) consists of Middle Minoan (E4). (Hood, 1971)

In First Order Logic of the inverse property:
- P9(x,y) ⇒ E4(x)
- P9(x,y) ⇒ E4(y)
- P9(x,y) ⇒ P10(y,x)
- [P9(x,y) ∧ P9(y,z)] ⇒ P9(x,z)
- P9(x,y) ⇒ ¬P9(y,x)
"""@en ;
    sh:name "P9i bildet Teil von"@de,
        "P9i αποτελεί μέρος του/της"@el,
        "P9i forms part of"@en,
        "P9i fait partie de"@fr,
        "P9i faz parte de"@pt,
        "P9i являeтся частью"@ru,
        "P9i 组成部分"@zh ;
    sh:nodeKind sh:BlankNodeOrIRI ;
    sh:path <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P9i_forms_part_of> .

